{
  "findings": [
    {
      "type": "surrogate_theorem",
      "statement": "Let s_0=0 and s_j=x_1+...+x_j, with s_n=0. For the rotation beginning after index k, 0<=k<n, its j-step partial sum equals s_{(k+j) mod n}-s_k, using periodicity s_{m+n}=s_m. As j ranges from 1 to n, the referenced residues range over all indices 0,...,n-1 exactly once. Hence N_k=#{0<=l<n:s_l>=s_k}. If s_0,...,s_{n-1} are distinct, their descending ranks are 1,...,n, so {N_k:0<=k<n}={1,...,n} exactly."
    },
    {
      "type": "rotation_average",
      "statement": "Therefore, for lambda>0, (1/n) sum_{k=0}^{n-1} exp(-lambda N_k)=(1/n) sum_{m=1}^n exp(-lambda m)=exp(-lambda)(1-exp(-lambda n))/(n(1-exp(-lambda))). In particular this is at most exp(-lambda)/(n(1-exp(-lambda)))."
    },
    {
      "type": "ties",
      "statement": "Distinctness is essential for the exact uniform-rank conclusion. With ties and the weak inequality >=, if the distinct partial-sum levels have ascending multiplicities a_1,...,a_t, then every rotation based at level i has N=a_i+...+a_t, and that value occurs a_i times. Thus the average is (1/n) sum_i a_i exp(-lambda(a_i+...+a_t)), not generally the uniform-rank formula."
    },
    {
      "type": "scale_explanation",
      "statement": "For an exchangeable bridge grouped into n equal coarse blocks, cyclic rotations have the same law. Conditional on a realization with distinct coarse boundary sums, averaging over the rotation index gives O(1/n). If each block has length L=floor(c log R) and the bridge has order R elementary positions, then n is order R/L, so this mechanism yields O(L/R)=O(log R/R), not O(1/R)."
    },
    {
      "type": "scope_limitation",
      "statement": "This is only a rank/rotation surrogate. It does not establish the actual Collatz-array marked-block bound: the useful-block event also requires a nonlow z entry, bounded positive pair totals, nonresonance, disjointness, and potentially a separate exact first-passage-conditioned law. No transfer of exchangeability or distinct boundary sums to that model has been supplied."
    }
  ],
  "claim_status": "OPEN; the cyclic-rank surrogate is proved, but GRID-AUDIT for the actual reference model is not resolved.",
  "first_missing_step": "Prove under the actual composition-bridge law, and separately under any required first-passage conditioning, a quantitative occupation statement connecting coarse rotations to the full useful-block event C_q with enough strength to improve the natural log(R)/R surrogate scale to C/R.",
  "unexpected_findings": [
    {
      "escalation_candidate": "Equal coarse blocks of logarithmic length intrinsically leave only about R/log R cyclic ranks, so the bare rotation argument produces log(R)/R rather than the requested 1/R."
    },
    {
      "escalation_candidate": "Ties in coarse boundary sums invalidate the exact uniform distribution of N unless separately excluded or controlled."
    }
  ]
}
